WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.240
In a dish, cut a neuron's axon close to the cell body, and one of its dendrites can

2
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.020
grow out as a new axon.

3
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.180
Cut the axon farther away, and the old axon regrows.

4
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.640
So an axon is not a permanent label.

5
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.800
What decides which process becomes the axon, and what keeps it that way?

6
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.680
Start in a dish. A rat hippocampal neuron grows several short neurites, and they all

7
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.500
look alike. After a day or two, one neurite starts to grow much faster than the

8
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.380
rest. That neurite becomes the axon.

9
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.960
After axon cuts, a neurite tended to win once it was about 10 micrometres longer.

10
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.980
The choice behaves like a race.

11
00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:48.563
A race with one winner needs two kinds of feedback.

12
00:00:49.403 --> 00:00:52.563
Positive feedback in the leader makes it grow faster the more it grows.

13
00:00:53.083 --> 00:00:56.263
A lipid called PIP3 builds up at its tip.

14
00:00:56.823 --> 00:01:01.363
Blocking PI3 kinase is reported to stop any neurite from becoming an axon.

15
00:01:01.983 --> 00:01:03.863
Negative feedback holds the others back.

16
00:01:04.343 --> 00:01:06.083
How it does that is less settled.

17
00:01:06.967 --> 00:01:10.007
Look at the growth cone, the moving tip of the leader.

18
00:01:10.627 --> 00:01:13.147
Its actin network is looser than in its siblings.

19
00:01:13.847 --> 00:01:18.867
Loosened actin is proposed to let microtubules push in, and the microtubules there

20
00:01:18.867 --> 00:01:24.167
are more stable. Loosen the actin in a chosen neurite, or stabilize its

21
00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:27.247
microtubules, and that neurite can become the axon.

22
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.660
Once chosen, the axon has to be held.

23
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.580
Near the cell body, a scaffold called ankyrin G builds the axon initial segment.

24
00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.080
It works as a gate.

25
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.800
Lower ankyrin G in a mature neuron, and the segment falls apart.

26
00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:48.800
A dendrite protein called MAP2 spreads into the near end of the axon, which begins

27
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.080
to look like a dendrite.

28
00:01:50.833 --> 00:01:52.353
Now return to the cut.

29
00:01:52.793 --> 00:01:58.633
In culture, leave a stump shorter than 35 micrometres, and little stable axon is

30
00:01:58.633 --> 00:02:03.313
left. It is a little like the first race again, and a dendrite can win it.

31
00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:06.693
Leave a longer stump, and the old axon regrows.

32
00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:10.913
Keep this rule. An axon is a state the cell holds.

33
00:02:10.913 --> 00:02:14.893
If enough of it is lost, that state can pass to another process.
